# ============================================================
# ILH Audits — GitHub CODEOWNERS
# ============================================================
#
# This file defines who must review and approve pull requests
# that touch specific parts of the codebase. GitHub will
# automatically request reviews from the listed owners when
# a PR modifies files matching these patterns.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
# Since the repository is public, this prevents unauthorized
# or unreviewed changes from reaching the main branch.
# The CTO, founder, or designated lead must approve all changes.
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
# - Each line specifies a file/directory pattern and the GitHub
#   username(s) who own that code.
# - The LAST matching pattern takes precedence.
# - Requires "Require review from Code Owners" to be enabled
#   in the branch protection rules (see branch-protection-guide.md).
# ============================================================

# ── Default owner for ALL files in the repository ──
# Every pull request requires approval from the project lead.
*                                   @abdaahads

# ── Critical Infrastructure — Database & Auth ──
# These files control data security, RLS policies, and
# authentication flows. Changes here can expose student
# data or break login. Extra scrutiny required.
supabase/                           @abdaahads
src/lib/supabase/                   @abdaahads
src/middleware.ts                   @abdaahads

# ── Environment & Secrets Configuration ──
# Prevent accidental commits of API keys or secret values.
.env*                               @abdaahads
